      "texte_contexte": "The superintendent of the US Naval Academy, Vice Admiral Walter “Ted” Carter, stated that the school could produce female Navy SEALs if the military changes its policy to allow women in special operations roles. Commander of the navy’s special warfare units, Rear Admiral Brian Losey, noted no insurmountable obstacles to opening the jobs to women. Defense Secretary Ash Carter is expected to receive final recommendations. In August, two women completed US Army Ranger School as part of a pilot program. The US marine corps released a study on combat units, which was criticized by navy secretary Ray Mabus.",
